For EXPRESSION=foo, this will grep for 'foo', *including* the single
quotes. You need to eval the string to have the single quotes be
interpreted.

RESULT="$(eval ${COMMAND} -E \'${EXPRESSION}\' ${CHECK_FILE} 2>/dev/null)"

Should do the trick.

